    LLM: 'Game: Three Card Brag. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Teen Patti (तीन पत्ती), meaning "three cards" in Hindi, is a popular Indian vying game that combines elements of poker and bluffing. Also known as **Flash** or **Three Card Brag**, it is one of the most widely played card games in the Indian subcontinent. The game is traditionally played during festivals, especially Diwali, and has gained international recognition through online gaming platforms.',
    objective: 'Win the pot by having the best three-card hand or by being the last player remaining after all others have folded.',
    gameplay: '1. Ante/Boot Phase\nAll players place the agreed minimum stake (boot) into the pot\nThis ensures there is something to play for in each hand',
    keyRules: [
      'Blind Player: Has not looked at their cards',
      'Must bet at least the current stake (minimum) or up to twice the current stake (maximum)',
      'Can bet less than a seen player',
      'Seen Player: Has looked at their cards',
      'Must bet at least twice the current stake (minimum) or up to four times the current stake (maximum)',
      'Must bet double what a blind player bets',
